# Left out of the set (the Kconfig options of drm618/README leave them out):
#   display/intel_display_debugfs.c, display/intel_display_debugfs_params.c, gt/intel_gt_debugfs.c, gt/intel_gt_engines_debugfs.c, gt/intel_gt_pm_debugfs.c, gt/intel_sseu_debugfs.c, gt/uc/intel_gsc_uc_debugfs.c, gt/uc/intel_guc_debugfs.c, gt/uc/intel_guc_log_debugfs.c, gt/uc/intel_huc_debugfs.c, gt/uc/intel_uc_debugfs.c, i915_debugfs.c, i915_debugfs_params.c: debugfs only (no debugfs in the layer; the 5.6 port left them out); CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is off
#   i915_hwmon.c: CONFIG_HWMON is off (the header has static inline stubs under IS_REACHABLE)
#   i915_pmu.c: CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS is off (stubs in i915_pmu.h)
#   intel_gvt.c, intel_gvt_mmio_table.c: CONFIG_DRM_I915_GVT is off (stubs in intel_gvt.h; the second needs gvt/reg.h)
#   i915_gpu_error.c: CONFIG_DRM_I915_CAPTURE_ERROR is off (stubs in i915_gpu_error.h): GPU hang diagnostics are lost, see README
#   gt/st_shmem_utils.c, gt/hsw_clear_kernel.c, gt/ivb_clear_kernel.c: not translation units: included by shmem_utils.c (self test) and gen7_renderclear.c (data)
#   display/intel_dp_tunnel.c: CONFIG_DRM_I915_DP_TUNNEL is off (static inline stubs in the header)
#   display/intel_opregion.c: CONFIG_ACPI is off (stubs in the header); the opregion and the VBT from it return with intel_acpi
#   display/intel_pipe_crc.c: CONFIG_DEBUG_FS is off (the header stubs the whole interface)
#   display/intel_fbdev.c, display/intel_fbdev_fb.c: CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION is off (stubs in intel_fbdev.h); the console on i915 is a question of the fbdev client of the DRM core
#   i915_ioc32.c: CONFIG_COMPAT is off (stubs in i915_ioc32.h): no 32 bit ioctls of the driver
#   i915_mm.c: remap_io_mapping and remap_io_sg walk page tables of a Linux mm; the 5.6 port built no such file; to be written over remap_pfn_range of the layer
#   display/intel_lpe_audio.c: Valleyview and Cherryview HDMI audio through a Linux platform device; the 5.6 port had a stub; the header stubs are for the xe build only
#   gt/intel_region_lmem.c: local memory of discrete cards (resizable BAR, PCI bus walk); the 5.6 port had a stub; not on an integrated GPU
#   gt/intel_gsc.c: the creation of the MEI auxiliary devices of the GSC; no MEI bus here
#   display/vlv_dsi.c: Valleyview tablets (DMI table with driver_data, the layer's dmi_system_id has none); the 5.6 port had a stub
